      "title": "Learning Not to Fool Yourself",
      "gist": "Scientists repeatedly bias their own measurements, as with Millikan's electron charge, so integrity means actively hunting for your own errors and publishing inconvenient results, even to laymen and politicians.",
      "question": "self-deception — how can scientists guard against unconsciously skewing their own results? (a historical case, three extensions)"
    },
