      "title": "Case Studies in Scientific Rigor",
      "gist": "Comparing careless rat and particle-physics experiments against Young's meticulous rat-corridor study shows true rigor means ruling out every possible cue, not merely getting the expected result.",
      "question": "rigor — what distinguishes sloppy experiments from one that truly controls for every variable? (contrasting case studies)"
    },
